data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":346,"item_id":"fc_04de6b92baab60ea016adb422c08b48191882f764450a240dc","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy: complete revised spec/graph submission\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The graph revision is not yet complete, so I cannot honestly submit a canonical artifact or claim the requested repairs were checked. In particular, R004 still needs to be rewritten around the recovered bilinear Frechet integration-by-parts theorem and its three integrability plus support-relative derivative hypotheses, with N001 as a direct input; the measure-preserving/Fubini branch should be removed rather than retained as unused sources. N001, R002/R003, ambient definitions and the R001 zero-integral derivation also need edits and structural validation. No substantive mathematical gap is asserted: these are concrete unfinished source and drafting obligations.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Actual task documents and findings; exact M011 theorem signature from successful probe_library and official Mathlib source lines 1–100. Search for compact-finiteness volume theorem returned no match; no substitute theorem is asserted.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Read SKILL and NL0 stage/format/self-containment/authoring/Audit A guidance; read frozen-target.md, problem.md, source-context.md, recovered-library-source.json, prior-candidate.json through the relevant graph and proof-source sections, and audit-findings.json including the independent R001–R003 findings. Probed M011 integral_bilinear_hasFDerivAt_right_eq_neg_left_of_integrable in Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.LineDeriv.IntegrationByParts (theorem, pinned commit and source hash returned); inspected its official source introduction. No artifact has been checked or submitted, and no Audit A PASS is claimed.\\\"}\"}"}

